# ============================================================================================
# B6 — THE TWO RUNG-9b BLOBS, byte-verified against an INDEPENDENT ASSEMBLER
# ============================================================================================
# ⭐ THE ORACLE IS TWO ASSEMBLERS ON THE SAME SOURCE. `kernel/shaders/edge_setup.s` and
# `edge_cov.s` are assembled by `llvm-mc -mcpu=gfx90c`; the identical instruction stream is
# emitted here through mabda's encoder and this file's label pass, and the two are byte-diffed.
# Neither side can be wrong alone without the diff saying so.
#
# ⛔ THE BRANCHES ARE THE POINT. llvm-mc RESOLVES the labels; edgeasm resolves them through
# ea_label/ea_branch/ea_fixup. So this diff verifies the fixup arithmetic against an
# independent implementation on SEVEN real branches (two backward loops in setup, three
# backward and two forward in cov) — not on the synthetic pair gate 2 uses. A blob with three
# backward branches and hand-counted offsets is exactly the silent-corruption case B4 exists
# to eliminate, and this is where that claim is actually tested.
#
# ⚠ The emit list was DERIVED from llvm-mc's own output through the encoder's field formulas,
# not transcribed from the .s by eye. [[feedback_audit_re_derive_dont_validate_comments]]
# 320 slots. ⚠ MEASURED, not assumed: module-scope `var X[N]` in a top-level program in this
# directory allocates N x u64 (a probe put two arrays 2048 bytes apart for X[256]). tri_rgba is 269
# dwords, so the old 256 would have overrun by 13 slots into whatever follows.
